cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use FiberBrowser in published work, please cite it as below, and cite
  FiberHMM, which calls the footprints FiberBrowser shows.
type: software
title: "FiberBrowser: a genome browser for single-molecule chromatin data (Fiber-seq and DAF-seq)"
version: 3.0.1
date-released: "2026-10-16"
authors:
  - name: "FiberBrowser Authors"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fiberseq/FiberBrowser"
url: "https://github.com/fiberseq/FiberBrowser"
abstract: >-
  FiberBrowser shows single DNA molecules from Fiber-seq (m6A) and DAF-seq
  (deamination) data with their chromatin footprints, clusters and sorts reads
  by their footprints at a locus, displays structural variants and the
  chromatin inside insertions, and exports figures and data. Footprints are
  called by FiberHMM.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - chromatin
  - fiber-seq
  - DAF-seq
  - genome-browser
  - single-molecule
  - footprinting
references:
  - type: software
    title: "FiberHMM: chromatin footprint calling from single-molecule Fiber-seq and DAF-seq data"
    version: 3.0.2
    authors:
      - name: "FiberHMM Authors"
    license: MIT
    repository-code: "https://github.com/fiberseq/FiberHMM"
    url: "https://fiberseq.github.io/FiberHMM/"
